<TextPage
	title="Privacy — Hookd"
	description="This site sets no cookies, has no accounts and no tracking. What little is processed, and by whom."
	heading="Privacy"
	updated="Last updated 19 August 2026"
>
	<p>
		This site is a set of static pages. There are no accounts, no comments, no contact form and
		no newsletter, so there is nothing for you to sign up to and nothing of yours to store.
	</p>

	<p>
		<strong>No cookies are set and no analytics are used.</strong> You are not tracked here,
		and nothing about your visit is stored in your browser.
	</p>

	<h2>Who else is involved</h2>

	<p>
		The site is hosted by <strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which processes ordinary request data —
		your IP address, the time, the page you asked for — in order to serve the page and to
		block abuse. Every website has this.
	</p>

	<p>
		Typefaces load from <strong>Google Fonts</strong>, so your browser contacts Google and
		Google sees your IP address as part of that request. It is the only third party this site
		reaches out to.
	</p>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>

	<p>
		Under the GDPR you can ask what personal data is held about you, have it corrected or
		erased, and complain to your national data protection authority. In practice I hold none,
		so there is nothing to send you — but if you think otherwise, ask and I will look.
	</p>

	<h2>Links out</h2>

	<p>
		Links to Ravelry, Instagram, Pinterest and yarn suppliers lead to sites with their own
		policies. This one does not cover them.
	</p>
</TextPage>
